  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c0c1416d-1629-5341-a8f3-95cf7fafb49f" activityNameId="a4c3420f-a001-5591-83e5-faa5764d907e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Maintenance, goods wagon</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Maintenance, goods wagon
The values are obtained top down, using the overall yearly consumption of service garages and the number of goods wagons owned by the SBB (19791 in 2000) . In order to allocate the maintenance expenditures between locomotives and wagons, we allocate 95% of the maintenance expenditures to wagon maintenance and 5% to locomotive maintenance. This al-location is based on the average vehicle weight (the weight of a locomotive is 3 times higher than an average wagon) and the number of vehicles in the rail equipment. ;
UUID: 43a8ae30-553e-3e48-96b7-01c0cfe942b9
This inventory includes energy processes (electricity, oil, natural gas and coal) which are obtained from service garages in Switzerland. Furthermore material expenditures for break shoes, lubricates and paint  are included. Also, the disposal of wood and sludge is addressed. Land use and material expenditures due to buildings of service garages are not included.
Location: Maintenance data reflect the situation in Switzerland 
Technology: The data represent current maintenance standards.
Time period: The energy data represents conditions in 2001. For some materials data from 1993 has been employed.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Maintenance expenditures for all SBB service garages available in form of oral communication. 
Extrapolations: Data from the Swiss Rail Company is used as an estimate for Europe
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_43a8ae30-553e-3e48-96b7-01c0cfe942b9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
